.TH TINCAN 1 "2026-11-16" "Tincan 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tincan \- lightweight SIP softphone for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tincan
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ target ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tincan
is a small SIP softphone with a compact window, a dial pad, a system tray
icon and desktop notifications. It supports several SIP accounts, calls with
hold, mute, transfer, local conference and recording, contacts with presence,
call history and SIP MESSAGE chat. SIP signalling and media are handled by
PJSIP.
.PP
Only one instance runs per user session. Starting
.B tincan
again forwards the target or command to the running instance and exits;
starting it without arguments brings the existing window to the front.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I target
A phone number or a
.BR sip: ,
.BR sips: ,
.B tel:
or
.B callto:
URI to dial with the default account. Spaces, dashes and brackets in
numbers are removed before dialling.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of the options and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help\-all
Also show the generic Qt options and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the Tincan and PJSIP versions and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-answer
Answer the ringing call.
.TP
.B \-\-hangup
Hang up the active call.
.TP
.B \-\-show
Show the window of the running instance.
.TP
.B \-\-quit
Quit the running instance.
.TP
.B \-\-minimized
Start hidden in the system tray.
.TP
.B \-\-null\-audio
Use the PJSIP null audio device instead of real sound hardware. Useful for
testing and on machines without audio devices.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tincan/tincan.ini
Settings and SIP accounts (default
.IR ~/.config/tincan/tincan.ini ).
Passwords are not written here; see
.BR SECURITY .
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/tincan/tincan.sqlite
Contacts, call history and chat messages (default
.IR ~/.local/share/tincan/ ).
.TP
.I $XDG_MUSIC_DIR/Tincan
Default folder for call recordings (WAV).
.SH SECURITY
Account passwords are stored with the desktop's Secret Service
(GNOME Keyring, KWallet and compatible) through QtKeychain. If no Secret
Service is available, Tincan asks before storing a password in a file
readable only by the user.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QT_QPA_PLATFORM
Selects the Qt platform plugin, for example
.B offscreen
for headless use.
.TP
.B LANG
Selects the user interface language when a translation is available.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success,
.B 1
if the SIP engine cannot start or the running instance cannot be reached,
.B 2
on invalid command-line arguments.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B tincan sip:200@pbx.example.com
Call extension 200 on pbx.example.com.
.TP
.B tincan tel:+15551234567
Call a telephone number through the default account.
.TP
.B tincan \-\-answer
Answer the incoming call from a keyboard shortcut or script.
